      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Twenty-three patients with angiographically documented total occlusion of the left main coronary artery were retrospectively identified. Statistical analysis suggests that poor right-to-left collaterals and the presence of concurrent significant right coronary artery disease were weakly associated with decreased survival after bypass surgery."},
